    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d481-a4">

                <pb facs="1306" n="1300" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg1300"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">General
                        Order</hi>,<lb/>No. 2.</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pacific Station,<lb/>Flagship Philadelphia</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Honolulu, Hawaiian Islands</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1894-11-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November 29, 1893</hi>.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The commander in chief calls the attention of all under his command to the
                    manifest impropriety of taking sides with either political party in Hawaii.</p>
                <p>The expression of political opinion or the wearing of badges is strictly
                    forbidden.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Irwin</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Rear-Admiral, U. S. Navy,<lb/>Commanding U. S. Naval
                            Force on Pacific Station.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
